# KavinEngine patches for lichess-bot (upstream commit df7e730, version 2026.8.9.2). Apply with `git apply` in the
# lichess-bot checkout; check with tools/test_lichess_bot_patch.py and lichess-bot's own `pytest test_bot`.
#  1. play_game: reopen a dropped game stream while lichess still lists the game (lost on time with 10 min left).
#  2. running_games: a repeated gameStart for a game whose thread runs starts no second thread.
#  3. accept_challenges: withdraw our pending challenge before accepting one (two games at once).
#  4. matchmaking: skip bots that are in a game (they can only decline; ~40 % of picks).
#  5. reconcile_games: once a minute, make the local game slots agree with lichess.org (resume games without a
#     thread, free slots of games that never started). This is the general fix for the bugs 1-3 are instances of.
#  6. play_game: engines of non-tournament games run at nice 10, so an arena game that starts during another game
#     gets the CPU (lichess-bot plays both; the 2026-10-09 arena draw vs caiporaBot shared the CPU with a rapid game).

